-- 141: 80s POP MINING — TUNEPILE HOOKS, REBUILT AROUND A SYNCOPATED KICK,
-- THEN STRIPPED BACK TO A SOLO MELODY.
-- Started as a 120 BPM groove with hooks mined from ~/tunepile
-- (index/tunepile.db, FTS5). The kick became the figure "x x - - x x x - -"
-- (9 steps) and everything was reworked around it; then kick + clap were
-- dropped, and finally all parts except the melody were dropped for a synth
-- solo, extended to an 8-bar passage (four 2-bar phrases) so it plays out
-- instead of looping every two bars.
--   * melody (d6)    — a-ha, "Take On Me" (1985)
--       tabs-tidal/Emil_Bulls_-_Take_On_Me.gp3-*.tidal (first-note extract).
--       Now an 8-bar arc: index phrase, a lift (up a 4th, cs6 peak), a
--       descending resolution, then a return to the head. Ramped forward
--       (gain slow 16, 0.62..1.15 saw) — it kept getting buried.
-- Hooks used earlier in the session and now silent, for the record:
--   arpeggio (d5) — Tears For Fears, "Everybody Wants To Rule The World"
--   bass     (d4) — Michael Jackson, "Billie Jean" contour, on dubsynth
--   pad      (d11) — vi-IV-I-V in F#m (Tunepile chords/progressions), hoRhodes
-- Claps: wet -> modulated -> dry -> dropped. Kick: 9-step figure -> dropped.
-- Delay: tap/dub delay removed (ddSend 0) from all melodic parts.
-- Sources: bd/hh/ho Dirt-Samples + dubsynth, hoRhodes (project DSP).
-- Mix: per-stream gain deliberate, master UNITY as in 139/140.
-- Verification: recording recordings/jam-20261004-1103.wav with change markers.
setcps 0.5

d1 $ silence

d2 $ silence

d3 $ silence

d4 $ silence

d5 $ silence

d6 $ slow 2 $ note "<[fs5 cs5 a4 e5 fs5 fs5 d5 b4 b4 e5 e5 gs5 gs5 a5 ~ ~] [a5 e5 cs5 fs5 a5 a5 f5 d5 d5 fs5 fs5 b5 ~ cs6 ~ ~] [cs6 b5 a5 gs5 a5 fs5 e5 cs5 d5 b4 a4 gs4 a4 ~ ~ ~] [fs5 cs5 a4 e5 fs5 fs5 d5 b4 b4 e5 e5 gs5 gs5 a5 ~ ~]>" # s "hoRhodes" # gain (slow 16 $ range 0.62 1.15 saw) # cutoff 4300 # release 0.4 # ddSend 0

d7 $ silence

d8 $ silence

d9 $ silence

d10 $ silence

d11 $ silence

d12 $ silence
